# scripts/check-legacy-naming.allowlist — exceptions for the rename
# verification script (0.31.0 lode/cairn/echo/sigil/stones; 0.50.0
# swarmcast/swarmgit/swarmresolve/swarmreg → filecast/gitback/hostdox/curator).
#
# Format:
#   <path>:<line>:<token>   exact-line allowlist
#   <path>:*:<token>        whole-file allowlist (ignore every match in this file)
#
# Lines starting with '#' and blank lines are comments.
# The third field is the matched token regex as printed by the script
# (e.g. `\bcairn\b`, `/var/lib/vigo/cairn\b`).
#
# Add a line here only when the legacy term is genuinely unavoidable —
# typically: historical commit messages preserved in completed.md, the
# user's literal disk-layout path (~/cairn/...), or test fixtures that
# deliberately probe the legacy terminology.

# completed.md is the historical record — every entry there is from
# before its surrounding rename and stays as-it-was for accuracy.
.claude/projects/-home-dan-cairn-vigo/memory/completed.md:*:cairn

# Memory files live outside the repo working tree (in
# ~/.claude/projects/...) so `git ls-files` doesn't return them.
# Listed here as a safety net in case future tooling brings them in.

# Dan's literal dev-repo directory is ~/swarmgit/{vigo,tessera,vigo-web}.
# Neither the 0.31.0 nor the 0.50.0 rename moves it on disk; they only
# rename the code-side per-user convention (~/gitback/<project>/ after
# 0.50.0). The CLAUDE.md lines below point at where tessera / vigo-web
# actually live, so the ~/swarmgit/ token there is intentional.
CLAUDE.md:56:\bswarmgit\b
CLAUDE.md:65:\bswarmgit\b
CLAUDE.md:141:\bswarmgit\b
CLAUDE.md:143:\bswarmgit\b

# The rename plan documents describe their renames — every legacy term
# appears as part of the mapping description. Allowlisted wholesale.
internal.docs/plan-substrate-rename.md:*:cairn
internal.docs/plan-rename-2026-05.md:*:swarmgit

# The France GTM plan lists "Cairn" as a product name in its glossary
# section; that prose was authored before the rename. Future pass.
internal.docs/plan-france-linux-migration-gtm.md:*:cairn

# multi-axis-audit.md references the memory directory absolute path
# `-home-dan-cairn-vigo` (Dan's literal workstation path).
internal.docs/multi-axis-audit.md:*:cairn

